## Note to the project owner

This is a starting point, not legal advice — if you're actively selling
this to clients, it's worth having an actual lawyer review (or draft) both
this license and the commercial/service agreement you put in front of
clients, particularly around data ownership, liability, and what happens
to a client's data if they stop paying or you stop supporting them.

If you'd instead prefer to open-source this project, replace this file
with a standard license such as MIT or Apache 2.0 (both are short,
well-understood, and widely trusted) — just be aware that doing so would
let anyone, including competitors, use and resell the code freely, which
is the opposite of what the proprietary terms above are meant to prevent.
